course: dictionary
lesson: 2694
title: Different means not the same
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Different» means not the same. A cat and a dog are different animals, because they are not alike. Try the swap: put "not the same" in place of "different", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Different» can also mean separate or another, as in «on different days». It can also mean unusual. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Use «different from» when you compare two things. «British Sign Language (BSL) is a full language with its own grammar, different from English.» The sentence tells you BSL and English are not the same. British speakers may say «different to» and American speakers «different than», but the meaning is the same.
explain: Sometimes «different» depends on where you are. «"On time" means different things in different places.» The meaning changes from place to place, so the word does not have one fixed meaning everywhere.
fact: «Different» means not the same.
fact: «Different» can mean separate or another, as in «on different days».
fact: «Different» can also mean unusual.
fact: «Stars have different colours»: the hottest are blue-white, our Sun is yellow-white, and cooler stars are orange or red.
fact: In animation, each picture is «a tiny bit different» from the one before, and your brain blends them into movement.
exercise: «Stars have different colours.» What does different mean here? | *Not the same | The same | Written down | Very hot
exercise: British Sign Language is «different from English». What does different from show? | *Two things are not the same | Something is very cold | Two things are exactly alike | Something is written in a book
exercise: Animation pictures are «each a tiny bit different». What does this mean? | Every picture is exactly the same | *Each picture is slightly changed from the one before | Each picture is in a frame on the wall | Each picture is very large
test: «On time» means different things in different places. What does different show? | The meaning is the same everywhere | The phrase is always spelt wrongly | Nobody uses the phrase | *The meaning changes from place to place
test: Dan says his pet snake is different. He means it is unusual. Which word has the same meaning as different here? | *Unusual | Same | Ordinary | Hungry
exam: In «BSL is a full language with its own grammar, different from English», what does different from mean? | Written in English | *Not the same as English | The same as English | Easier than English
